<!--
  The breaking-change inventory for this release. Generated, never hand-written
  (dotnet pack -p:ApiCompatGenerateSuppressionFile=true), which also means a regeneration drops this
  comment and the CRLF it writes needs normalising back to LF. Five entries, all deliberate:

  CP0002 x1 WithGuards(int, int, int, int): the all-int overload went when the four guards became
  int?, so naming one stopped silently resetting the other three to the engine constants.

  CP0014 x2 PaginateComposedQuery<TEntity>.SortBy: the property and its getter lost their nullable
  annotation when a tie-breaker became mandatory at Build(), so an empty list now unambiguously means
  "resolved, nothing requested".

  CP0014 x2 PaginateLinkContext.Equals / GetHashCode: both were synthesized by the record and are now
  hand-written, so they no longer carry CompilerGeneratedAttribute. The members and their behaviour
  are what changed on purpose — the attribute is a side effect of writing them out.

  All four CP0014 appear only because the ApiCompat attribute rule is now on: annotations and
  compiler-generated markers live in metadata the signature comparison does not read, and
  PublicAPI.Shipped.txt records a member only as line text. Each of these went in with no diagnostic
  from anything before that rule was enabled.

  Delete this file when PackageValidationBaselineVersion moves past 10.0.3: every entry exists only
  against that baseline, and a stale suppression hides the next accidental break behind the same target.
-->
